# layer-contract-conformance-b is a shard driver: it execs the sibling layer-contract-conformance/run.sh --group b, and declares the parent's paths but ONE:
# the parent keys +CLAUDE.md, which a FIFO probe found read under the parent's run and not under this shard's.
# The validator walks the whole distribution tree and renders its arm map via render-invariant-index.sh --arm-lines <src>, which needs no root marker.
!scripts/validate-enforcement-map.sh
scripts/
# reason: core/ is walked by content -- the validator the parent run.sh runs (layer-contract-conformance/run.sh:750) finds every core/*.sh and derives core/*/, scripts/validate-enforcement-map.sh:2476 and :3327.
core/
templates/
.githooks/
patterns/
.claude/rules/
